{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2502 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e05d3f984e6733e47a4ec83ea15dc20af329f990349a3230b0f976a6e4259d5d" :edb/db-before-t 2501 :edb/db-after-t 2502 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535814 50 #inst "2026-10-14T23:29:35.580Z" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186078584 1038 #edb/ref 17592186529418 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186078584 1038 #edb/ref 17592186529434 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186078584 1038 #edb/ref 17592186529436 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186078584 1038 #edb/ref 17592186529438 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186078584 1038 #edb/ref 17592186529446 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186078584 1038 #edb/ref 17592186529448 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186078584 1038 #edb/ref 17592186529464 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186078584 1040 #edb/ref 17592186529466 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529417 1080 "18\\,\\text{min}" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529417 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529417 1083 #uuid "035a9a44-7a16-5905-a0dc-77a5358cf6b1" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529418 1068 #edb/ref 17592186529453 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529418 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529418 1071 "A heated metal body cools in a room at ${18}^{∘}\\text{C}.$ Its temperature is ${60}^{∘}\\text{C}$ after $3$ minutes and ${39}^{∘}\\text{C}$ after $7$ minutes. The temperature $T(t)$, in degrees Celsius, obeys Newton's law of cooling, with $t$ measured in minutes since cooling began. To the nearest minute, how long after cooling began does the body reach ${25}^{∘}\\text{C}$?" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529418 1072 #uuid "08518a50-98e2-5d9c-a6f5-59dc1a4a2277" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529418 1074 "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the inhibited decay equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-k(T-18),\\qquad k>0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dT}{T-18} & =-k\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dT}{T-18} & =-k\\int dt \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-18| & =-kt+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited decay equation, we have $T-18>0$ for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-18 & ={e}^{-kt+C} \\\\ T-18 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-kt} \\\\ T-18 & =K{e}^{-kt} \\\\ T & =18+K{e}^{-kt}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nApply the two observed conditions $T(3)=60$ and $T(7)=39$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}60 & =18+Ke^{-3k} \\\\ 42 & =Ke^{-3k} \\\\ 39 & =18+Ke^{-7k} \\\\ 21 & =Ke^{-7k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDivide the excess temperatures to eliminate $K$, then take natural logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{21}{42} & =\\frac{Ke^{-7k}}{Ke^{-3k}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =e^{-4k} \\\\ \\ln(\\frac{1}{2}) & =-4k \\\\ k & =\\frac{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow substitute this rate into $T(3)=60$ to determine the constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}42 & =Ke^{-3(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{4})} \\\\ K & =42e^{3(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{4})} \\\\ K & =42\\left(\\frac{42}{21}\\right)^{\\frac{3}{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution satisfying both observations is\n\n$$\nT(t)=18+42\\left(\\frac{42}{21}\\right)^{\\frac{3}{4}}e^{-(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{4})t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two observation times confirms the model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3) & =18+(42\\left(\\frac{42}{21}\\right)^{\\frac{3}{4}})e^{-(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{4})\\cdot 3}=60 \\\\ T(7) & =18+(42\\left(\\frac{42}{21}\\right)^{\\frac{3}{4}})e^{-(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{4})\\cdot 7}=39\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the body reaches ${25}^{∘}\\text{C}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({t}_{1}) & =25 \\\\ 18+Ke^{-k{t}_{1}} & =25 \\\\ Ke^{-k{t}_{1}} & =7 \\\\ e^{-k{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{7}{K} \\\\ -k{t}_{1} & =\\ln\\left(\\frac{7}{K}\\right) \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{k}\\ln\\left(\\frac{7}{K}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the values of $K$ and $k$ to obtain the time measured since cooling began:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{\\frac{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{4}}\\ln\\left(\\frac{7}{42\\left(\\frac{42}{21}\\right)^{\\frac{3}{4}}}\\right) \\\\ {t}_{1} & =3+4\\frac{\\ln(\\frac{1}{6})}{\\ln(\\frac{1}{2})}≈13\\,\\text{min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529419 1080 "30\\,\\text{min}" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529419 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529419 1083 #uuid "09046438-fbef-58e9-b053-5d1dfaf0a2ad" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529420 1080 "15\\,\\text{min}" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529420 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529420 1083 #uuid "0db77da5-938c-5d21-b72a-0f710e5c2a0b" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529421 1080 "42\\,\\text{min}" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529421 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529421 1083 #uuid "108ed220-ff0d-5a3e-9732-871db25e264d" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529422 1080 "13\\,\\text{min}" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529422 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529422 1083 #uuid "136b59f4-a9e4-5d8c-b869-dad46630033a" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529423 1080 "15\\,\\text{min}" 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529423 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535814 17592186045443 true] [17592186529423 1083 #uuid "14340294-f6e6-5843-a6fe-4ec754aa2b3a" 13194139535814 17592186045443 t